    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_83c7b97e",
      "@type": "AnalogicalMapping",
      "instance_name": "mapping_id_1",
      "label": "Black ants are mapped as 'slaves' in the text",
      "description": "The text 'some of my best slaves are black' explicitly maps the visual entity 'ants' (specifically black ants) onto the concept of 'slaves'. This is a direct analogical mapping where the visual material (black ants) is equated with enslaved Black people, reinforcing a dehumanizing and racist metaphor. The ants' laborious activity of carrying larvae is visually analogous to the historical and racist trope of enslaved people being treated as property or laborers.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
